{
  "$comment": [
    "ABOUTME: Network topology for the relayer (spec §7.2) — the single source of truth for which",
    "ABOUTME: chains exist per network and their fixed properties. Addresses live in the manifests.",
    "One hub + N clients per network. To add a client: append an entry to that network's `clients`",
    "array (chainId, CCTP domain, an rpcUrlEnv naming its endpoint var, poll cadence, confirmations,",
    "manifestPrefix = the monorepo flat-manifest filename stem). To run a subset of the configured",
    "clients, set ENABLED_CLIENTS (comma-separated chain `name`s); unset = all clients. The hub is",
    "always included. Both the watcher and actor read this file at boot from ${DEPLOYMENTS_DIR}.",
    "rpcUrlEnv convention: <SLUG_UPPERCASE>_RPC. Endpoint values are supplied via env (endpoints.env)."
  ],
